Enter your battery's address. Auto-discovery found: {found}

If nothing was found, Home Assistant probably can't reach the battery. It must be on the same network as Home Assistant, not a guest Wi-Fi. To check, type the battery's IP address into a browser on a device on Home Assistant's network. You should see an Energizer Homepower page.

The defaults below are the manufacturer's own published values and work on unmodified units. Leave the telemetry source on Automatic unless you have a reason not to: it reads the battery directly over your network, and switches to MQTT for units that need it. For the MQTT source, the broker host, credentials and topic serial are read from the battery automatically where possible.
